# Commits listed here are pure reformatting: they change whitespace and line
# breaks, never behaviour. `git blame` skips them and attributes each line to
# the commit that last changed its meaning.
#
# Turn it on once per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically, so its blame view already skips them.
#
# One caveat on the entry below. Pull requests land as a squash merge, so the
# reformat does not arrive on main as its own commit: it is folded together with
# the tooling change that introduced the formatter. Skipping this hash therefore
# also skips a handful of config lines. That is the right trade -- it hides 202
# reformatted files and hides nothing anyone blames a config file for.

